[scene name="AnisoRotation" version=1]
; Anisotropy-rotation test. Two identical brushed-metal spheres under one sharp
; sun (low ambient so the anisotropic highlight streak dominates). They differ
; ONLY in anisotropyRotation: LEFT = 0, RIGHT = 90 degrees (1.5708 rad). If
; rotation works, the elongated specular streak is oriented differently on the
; two spheres (rotated ~90 degrees relative to each other).

